// PARAM: --analysis interval
// random() gives x no bound at all (Top), but the guard on each branch
// narrows it before the check runs: the true arm's assume tightens x to
// [1,+inf), the false arm's to (-inf,0]. Both checks read back their own
// arm's narrowed range, not the pre-branch Top -- a guard/assume-narrowing
// regression, not a join regression (unlike 01-if_else.vimp, the check is
// inside each arm, before any post-if join). The false arm is phrased as
// x<1 rather than !(0<x): the latter is PROVED-able too in principle (same
// narrowed range decides it), but the check evaluator currently reports
// UNKNOWN for a NEGATED comparison against an unbounded-below range even
// where the direct comparison decides -- a separate, unconfirmed precision
// gap, not what this fixture is testing.
void main() {
  x := random();
  if (0 < x) {
    __voblint_check(0 < x) // PROVED
  } else {
    __voblint_check(x < 1) // PROVED
  }
}
